## 👤 Linux Users

A Linux system can have multiple users.

Each user can have different permissions and access to different files and resources.

There are usually two main types of users:

- Regular users
- Root user

### Root User

The root user has very high privileges and can perform administrative tasks on the system.

Because root has a lot of power, it should be used carefully.

## 👥 Linux Groups

Groups allow multiple users to share permissions.

For example, a group could be created for users who need access to the same files or resources.

Instead of giving permissions to every user individually, permissions can be assigned through groups.

## 📂 File Ownership

Linux files and directories have an owner and a group.

